          "type": "turn",
          "question": "Where do authorities differ on how lipid-treatment goals are expressed?",
          "answer": "Authorities differ in how they express lipid-treatment goals, particularly with regard to LDL targets. \n\nUnited States guidance typically does not specify numeric LDL targets. Instead, it focuses on statin intensity and the percentage reduction in LDL cholesterol from baseline levels. In contrast, European guidance specifies explicit LDL goals that vary by risk category, suggesting combination therapy when a statin alone is insufficient. This means that the definition of being \"at goal\" for lipid management can differ significantly depending on the guidance used (source: Major cardiology society consensus guidance).\n\nI cannot provide additional details beyond this comparison of LDL target expressions in different guidelines.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
